Register the framebuffer serial console once.
serial_init() runs again as long as it found no serial device (it returns without setting uart_initted), and the
second register_serial_functions() of the sweet-fbcon table made gPESF a cycle (next = itself). uart_getc() then never
returned: with boot-arg serial=3 the serial keyboard thread (serial_keyboard_poll, MAXPRI_KERNEL) spun in it from boot,
one CPU (an A55 mostly) at 100 % system time, the A55 cluster held at its top clock by the governor (2026-10-29: kernel
stackshot via sweetstackshot/kstack.py, uart_getc+0x20 <- _serial_getc <- serial_keyboard_poll).
diff --git a/pexpert/arm/pe_serial.c b/pexpert/arm/pe_serial.c
--- a/pexpert/arm/pe_serial.c
+++ b/pexpert/arm/pe_serial.c
@@ -872,6 +872,15 @@
 	uint32_t const *val;
 	unsigned int size;
 
+	/*
+	 * Once only (0255). serial_init() runs again as long as it found no serial device (it then returns without setting
+	 * uart_initted), and registering this table a second time made gPESF a cycle (next = itself): uart_getc() never
+	 * returned. With boot-arg serial=3 the serial keyboard thread (serial_keyboard_poll, MAXPRI_KERNEL) sat in it from
+	 * boot on, one CPU at 100 % system time (2026-10-29, kernel stackshot: uart_getc+0x20). fbcon_base is set only here.
+	 */
+	if (fbcon_base != NULL) {
+		return;
+	}
 	if (SecureDTFindEntry("name", "sweet-fbcon", &entry) != kSuccess ||
 	    SecureDTGetProperty(entry, "reg", (void const **)&reg, &size) != kSuccess || size < 16) {
 		return;
